# Realistic Space Simulation Physics Engine Implementation

## Core Principles of Orbital Mechanics

The physics engine is based on Newtonian mechanics, specifically Newton's Law of Universal Gravitation and the equations of motion for orbital systems. Key equations:

1. Gravitational Force Equation:
```cpp
F = G * (m1 * m2) / r²
```
Where:
- F is gravitational force
- G is gravitational constant (6.67430 × 10⁻¹¹ m³ kg⁻¹ s⁻²)
- m1 and m2 are masses of two bodies
- r is the distance between centers

2. Acceleration from Force:
```cpp
a = F / m
```

3. Equations of Motion:
```cpp
position(t+Δt) = position(t) + velocity(t) * Δt
velocity(t+Δt) = velocity(t) + acceleration(t) * Δt
```

## Core Physics Engine Implementation

```cpp
// physics_engine.cpp
#include "physics_engine.h"
#include <cmath>
#include <vector>
#include <stdexcept>

namespace space_simulation {

    // Constants
    const double G = 6.67430e-11; // Gravitational constant (m³ kg⁻¹ s⁻²)

    // Vector type definition
    typedef std::vector<double> Vector;

    // Calculate gravitational force between two bodies
    Vector calculateGravitationalForce(const Vector& position1, const Vector& position2, double mass1, double mass2) {
        // Calculate distance vector
        Vector distance = subtractVectors(position2, position1);

        // Calculate distance magnitude
        double distanceMagnitude = std::sqrt(dotProduct(distance, distance));

        // Calculate gravitational force magnitude
        double forceMagnitude = G * (mass1 * mass2) / std::pow(distanceMagnitude, 2);

        // Calculate direction vector
        Vector direction = normalizeVector(distance);

        // Calculate force vector
        Vector force = multiplyVectorByScalar(direction, forceMagnitude);

        return force;
    }

    // Calculate net gravitational force on a body
    Vector calculateNetGravitationalForce(const std::vector<std::pair<Vector, double>>& bodies, const Vector& position) {
        Vector netForce = {0, 0, 0}; // Assuming 3D space

        for (const auto& body : bodies) {
            if (body.first != position) { // Skip self-gravity
                Vector force = calculateGravitationalForce(position, body.first, 1.0, body.second);
                netForce = addVectors(netForce, force);
            }
        }

        return netForce;
    }

    // Update position and velocity using Euler integration
    void updateState(Vector& position, Vector& velocity, const Vector& acceleration, double deltaTime) {
        // Update velocity
        for (size_t i = 0; i < position.size(); ++i) {
            velocity[i] += acceleration[i] * deltaTime;
        }

        // Update position
        for (size_t i = 0; i < position.size(); ++i) {
            position[i] += velocity[i] * deltaTime;
        }
    }

    // Calculate gravitational forces between all bodies
    std::vector<Vector> calculateAllForces(const std::vector<std::pair<Vector, double>>& bodies) {
        std::vector<Vector> forces;

        for (const auto& body : bodies) {
            Vector force = {0, 0, 0};

            for (const auto& otherBody : bodies) {
                if (body.first != otherBody.first) { // Skip self-gravity
                    Vector f = calculateGravitationalForce(body.first, otherBody.first, 1.0, otherBody.second);
                    force = addVectors(force, f);
                }
            }

            forces.push_back(force);
        }

        return forces;
    }

    // Calculate orbital period using Kepler's Third Law
    double calculateOrbitalPeriod(double semiMajorAxis, double primaryMass) {
        return 2 * M_PI * std::sqrt(std::pow(semiMajorAxis, 3) / (G * primaryMass));
    }

    // Helper functions
    double dotProduct(const Vector& a, const Vector& b) {
        double result = 0.0;
        for (size_t i = 0; i < a.size(); ++i) {
            result += a[i] * b[i];
        }
        return result;
    }

    Vector addVectors(const Vector& a, const Vector& b) {
        Vector result;
        for (size_t i = 0; i < a.size(); ++i) {
            result.push_back(a[i] + b[i]);
        }
        return result;
    }

    Vector subtractVectors(const Vector& a, const Vector& b) {
        Vector result;
        for (size_t i = 0; i < a.size(); ++i) {
            result.push_back(a[i] - b[i]);
        }
        return result;
    }

    Vector multiplyVectorByScalar(const Vector& vector, double scalar) {
        Vector result;
        for (size_t i = 0; i < vector.size(); ++i) {
            result.push_back(vector[i] * scalar);
        }
        return result;
    }

    Vector normalizeVector(const Vector& vector) {
        Vector result;
        double magnitude = std::sqrt(dotProduct(vector, vector));

        if (magnitude == 0) {
            throw std::domain_error("Cannot normalize zero vector");
        }

        for (size_t i = 0; i < vector.size(); ++i) {
            result.push_back(vector[i] / magnitude);
        }

        return result;
    }

} // namespace space_simulation
```

